-- #119 주문 접수와 체결 (ADR-0107 결정 1 #177 2·3·7·8·9·11·12·15항, 결정 3 '주문 접수', 결정 5 '#119'
-- 행들; ADR-0111 결정 6·8; ADR-0112). Orders and fills take the CLOB's shape: an order is a quantity
-- or an IOC budget buy with a confirmed and a protected limit, an arrival key, its filled amounts
-- and one of six states with its reason, kept as a row when rejected; a fill is one match between
-- an incoming and a resting order with both owners and their account types, its price in the
-- incoming contract and the YES price; a market holds its 가격 보호 폭. Generated by `drizzle-kit
-- generate` (every reshaped column answered "create": the tables are empty), then hand-edited
-- where marked: this header, the guard, the rebuild of `order_status` in place of drizzle-kit's
-- ADD VALUE, and the tail. The snapshot matches the schema (a re-run of `generate` reports no
-- changes).
--
-- Not merge-wait class (2) (ADR-0107 결정 3): `orders`, `fills` and `positions` are empty in the
-- deployed database since 0060's wipe, and nothing has written them since (intake opens with
-- this migration, behind `order.accepting`). The guard below refuses to run on a database whose
-- orders or fills are not empty rather than delete them — see docs/RESET.md. The new NOT NULL
-- columns without a default need the empty tables; `markets` gains one nullable column, so no
-- market changes.
--
-- 1. The guard comes first. 2. `order_status` gains 만료 (`expired`) by a rebuild (column to text,
--    DROP TYPE, CREATE TYPE, cast back) on the empty table, as 0060 rebuilt `ledger_entry_type`:
--    a value added with ADD VALUE could not be used by a later statement of the same migrate run
--    (#120's). `order_type` and `counterparty_type` go with their columns. 3. The tail: the order
--    and fill records' triggers, the ledger events' binding to their fill and the width's fixing,
--    with the REVOKEs — buddha_app loses DELETE of `orders` and UPDATE and DELETE of `fills`.
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.orders) OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.fills) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '0062 reshapes orders and fills, which must be empty (0060 wiped them): see docs/RESET.md';
  END IF;
END
$$;--> statement-breakpoint
